<title>MOROCCO: Spain to build seven hospitals in Morocco.</title>
<headline>Spain to build seven hospitals in Morocco.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain plans to build seven hospitals in northern Morocco at a cost of $20 million over two years, the official MAP news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It quoted Senen Florensa, head of the Spanish Institute for Cooperation with the Arab World, as saying that Spain and Morocco had signed a health convention on the issue.</p>
<p>The hospitals will be on the Mediterranean coast where an estimated five million people live, it said.</p>
</text>
